abstract: >-
  PerceptFence proposes a content-layer mediation architecture for screen-share
  assistants. This blinded review artifact is a deterministic synthetic-fixture
  scaffold: fixture scenario labels drive fixed policy, redaction,
  per-invocation memory-gate, output, and in-memory audit actions. It does not
  implement live capture, authenticated re-consent, persistent cross-session
  memory, or an external model adapter. The artifact contains only invented
  fixtures and deterministic evaluation results; no real captures, personal
  data, customer data, human-subject data, or production telemetry.
